# Client-side routing: the browser asks for /cuentas, which is a route in the
# bundle and not a file in the upload. Without this Pages answers 404 — every
# deep link and every refresh away from `/` breaks, and only in the published
# app, never in `vite dev`. This is the CloudFront CustomErrorResponses rule
# in the form Pages reads.
#
# 200, not 302: the address bar has to keep the route the router is about to
# read. And it must stay last, below any real redirect, because the first
# matching rule wins.
/*  /index.html  200
